Ladybird ends an outside marker at the start of its list item’s border
box. Gecko’s nsBlockFrame::ReflowOutsideMarker() computes that same
offset: the content start, less the list item’s start border and
padding, less the marker’s end margin and its size. Blink places the
marker against the start of the border box in UnpositionedListMarker::
AddToBox(). And WebKit’s RenderListItem::placeExcludedMarker() moves it
there from the content edge, by subtracting borderAndPaddingStart().
Chrome and Firefox both draw it outside the border box in a manual
check: with start padding, with a start border, and right to left.
